# bundled node runtime for the packaged build (placed locally, not committed)
app/runtime/

# per-league personal data (real owner identities + draft history) -- never ship; the sim falls back
# to a generic field when absent (src/draft/managers.ts)
data/managers.json
data/owners.json
data/recaps.json
# The human-readable scouting report DERIVED from those three. It names real league members and
# characterises how each of them drafts, so it is exactly as personal as its inputs and belongs in
# the same bucket -- per install, never committed. It lived in docs/ until 2026-09-05 and was purged
# from history when the repo went public. Same pattern as data/cheatsheet.md: a generated markdown
# artifact that stays local.
data/league-managers.md

# derived per-league backtest history (scored under the league's own scoring model) -- rebuild with
# `ff build-history`; committing it would ship one league's scoring to everyone
data/history-points.csv
data/history-weekly.csv
data/rank-outcomes.json

